# Everything textual stays LF in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# This is not a style preference. The vendored Killer schema is hashed in three
# places -- stamp.json, the test that compares the two, and the CI drift check
# that re-fetches it from GitHub -- and it is embedded into the binary from the
# working-tree file. Without this, a fresh clone on Windows gets CRLF, every
# one of those hashes disagrees, and the failure reads as "the upstream
# contract moved" when nothing moved at all.
#
# The shell script needs LF for its own reasons: bash will not run a script
# whose shebang line ends in CR.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces on the file whose bytes are load-bearing.
internal/contract/killerschema/finding.schema.json text eol=lf
internal/contract/testdata/*.json                 text eol=lf
*.sh                                              text eol=lf
